-- title:
--   Self Consistency Restricted Average Eq
-- statement:
--   **Restricted self-consistency averages recover the ambient error.** Let `strategy` be a symmetric strategy for the successor parameters. For each slice height $x$, write $c(x)$ for the self-consistency failure probability of the restricted strategy, and write $C$ for the successor strategy's self-consistency failure probability. Then
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb E_{x\sim\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q)} c(x)=C.
--   $$
--
--   The equality is the distributional decomposition of a uniform successor point into a predecessor point and its final coordinate. It is used when assembling the ordinary and answer-valued restricted-probabilities statements, where the axis and diagonal branches pay the conditioning loss but the self-consistency branch does not.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.MainInductionStep.selfConsistencyRestrictedAverage_eq`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/MainInductionStep/Theorems/RestrictedProbabilities/Base.lean#L93-L115

